---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '../components/ui/Button.astro';
import TimelineItem from '../components/ui/TimelineItem.astro';
import Icon from '../components/ui/Icon.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Carol I. Zacheiss, Attorney at Law"
  description="34 years of criminal defense experience serving Hopewell, Prince George, Petersburg, Richmond, and Chesterfield, Virginia."
>
  <section class="section stack">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>Meet Carol I. Zacheiss.</h1>
    <p class="hero-copy">
      Carol has spent 34 years practicing criminal law, first as a prosecutor and, for decades
      since, as defense counsel &mdash; experience she now brings to every client she represents.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--panel grid-2 grid photo-intro">
    <img
      src="/images/headshot-smile.jpg"
      alt="Carol I. Zacheiss, Attorney at Law, smiling"
      width="1100"
      height="1650"
      decoding="async"
      class="portrait-photo"
    />
    <div class="stack">
      <p class="hero-copy">
        Carol was raised in the New York metropolitan area and began her legal career as a
        prosecutor in Brooklyn and the Bronx, where she spent her first seven years in the
        courtroom.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-copy">
        After relocating to the Richmond, Virginia area, she continued as a prosecutor with the
        Richmond City Commonwealth&rsquo;s Attorney&rsquo;s Office, handling violent crime cases
        &mdash; including robberies and firearm possession charges &mdash; and serving on the
        office&rsquo;s Domestic Violence Team.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-copy">
        That experience shaped what came next. Carol joined the Petersburg Public Defender&rsquo;s
        Office, drawn to representing people facing serious charges who might otherwise go without
        strong representation, and later helped open two new Public Defender&rsquo;s Offices in
        the Tidewater region before entering private practice.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-copy">
        Today, Carol&rsquo;s practice is devoted exclusively to criminal defense. She has deep
        experience with drug crime and firearms charges, Fourth Amendment search-and-seizure
        issues, criminal record expungement, restoration of gun rights, and protective order
        matters &mdash; representing clients throughout Hopewell, Prince George, Petersburg,
        Richmond, and Chesterfield.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-copy">
        Outside the office, Carol spends her time with family and friends, her two working dogs,
        and pursuits that keep her grounded &mdash; traveling, swimming, reading, cooking,
        gardening, and animal rescue.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section stack">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Experience</p>
      <h2>34 years, both sides of the courtroom.</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="timeline">
      <TimelineItem eyebrow="Early Career" title="Prosecutor in Brooklyn and the Bronx">
        Carol began her 34-year legal career as a prosecutor in the New York metropolitan area,
        spending her first seven years in the courtroom.
      </TimelineItem>
      <TimelineItem eyebrow="Richmond, Virginia" title="Prosecutor, Richmond City Commonwealth's Attorney's Office">
        After relocating to Virginia, Carol prosecuted violent crime cases, including robberies and
        firearm possession charges, and served on the office's Domestic Violence Team.
      </TimelineItem>
      <TimelineItem eyebrow="Petersburg" title="Petersburg Public Defender's Office">
        Carol moved to public defense to represent people facing serious charges who needed strong
        representation.
      </TimelineItem>
      <TimelineItem eyebrow="Tidewater" title="Helped open two new Public Defender's Offices">
        Carol helped launch two new Public Defender's Offices in the Tidewater region.
      </TimelineItem>
      <TimelineItem eyebrow="Today" title="Private criminal defense practice">
        Now in private practice, Carol represents clients across Hopewell, Prince George,
        Petersburg, Richmond, and Chesterfield &mdash; focused exclusively on criminal defense.
      </TimelineItem>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--frame stack">
    <span class="panel-icon"><Icon name="phone-call" /></span>
    <h2>Facing a criminal charge?</h2>
    <p class="hero-copy">
      Get direct, experienced counsel for your case throughout Hopewell, Prince George,
      Petersburg, Richmond, and Chesterfield.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <Button href="/contact" variant="solid">Request a Consultation</Button>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
